===Etymology===
{{ellipsis|ga|Béarla gallda|t=foreign speech}} from {{m|ga|béarla|t=speech, language}}, from {{der|ga|sga|bélrae}}, from {{m|sga|bél|t=mouth}}.<ref>{{R:DIL|5638|head=bélrae}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|author=anonymous<!--Arbuthnot, Ní Mhaonaigh and Toner are the authors of the book under discussion, not the authors of the newspaper article--> |url=https://www.irishtimes.com/culture/books/bearla-punt-fliuch-a-history-of-ireland-in-10-little-words-1.4069438 |title=Béarla, Punt, Fliuch: A history of Ireland in 10 little words |work=The Irish Times |date=2023-11-09 |accessdate=2024-05-01}}</ref> Compare {{cog|gd|Beurla Ghallta}}.

